{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "right-edge horizontal runs of the moving color, one run per occupied row",
  "path": "left along the same row through background cells, stopping immediately to the right of the nearest fixed barrier pixel or at the left edge if no barrier is present",
  "trajectory": "translate each whole run horizontally, preserving its length and color; rows are independent",
  "transform": "clear each run's original right-edge cells; keep fixed barrier pixels and rows without moving runs unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 6-9 rows x 6-9 cols
  colors: bg=0(black), barrier=8(azure), moving=3(green) [observed]; solver detects dynamically
  barrier:
    scattered pixels across the grid; density 0.29-0.41 of total cells
    present in both moving and non-moving rows; 0-5 per moving row, 1-7 per non-moving row
  moving_runs:
    1-2 contiguous rectangular groups of right-edge runs (each group has constant run_len)
    run_length: 1-2 per group; group_height: 2-4 rows
    total moving rows: 2-6; total moving cells: 4-9
    each run occupies columns [W-run_len, W-1] in the input
  slide_rule:
    each run slides left to pack against the nearest barrier in its row, or column 0 if none
    gap between nearest barrier and run start (=slide distance): 0-6; at least 1 row must slide >0
    gap cells (between target_start and original run start) are all background
  non_moving_rows: 3-5 rows with only bg and barrier; no pure-bg rows exist [observed]

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid H (6-9), W (6-9); pick 3 colors for bg, barrier, moving
    2. Decide 1-2 moving groups; for each, pick group_height (2-4) and run_len (1-2); assign row ranges (non-overlapping, separated by >=1 non-moving row)
    3. For each moving row, choose a target_start position (0 or barrier_col+1); place barrier pixels to the left of target_start randomly; place the moving run at [target_start, target_start+run_len-1] -- this is the OUTPUT
    4. Scatter barrier pixels in non-moving rows (density ~0.3-0.4), ensuring every non-moving row has >=1 barrier
    5. Verify at least one moving row has slide>0 (target_start < W-run_len); if not, adjust
    6. Derive INPUT: move each run from its output position to the right edge [W-run_len, W-1], filling vacated cells with bg; ensure no barrier occupies right-edge columns in moving rows
```
